====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  In plane symmetry, where MOND is exact and no boost model is needed, nonlinear MOND on baryons alone lifts the Silk-damped
  small-scale power by 100-1000x over Newton by z = 3 -- and still falls 1000-5000x short of what the forest measures, for any
  initial amplitude a baryon-only history can have.  The reason is the external-field effect the per-mode linear model ignored:
  the local field is set by the large-scale modes, so small scales inherit their boost, not their own.  With the framework's
  derived floor the boost is off entirely.  The forest side of the fermion hybrid is closed; the forest needs a component that
  clusters on 1-5 Mpc at z = 3, and that component sits in galaxies.  A 1-D proxy, but the shortfall is three orders, not a factor.

